{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>And you shall separate the children of Israel from their impurity.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory said: From here is a warning to the children of Israel that they must separate from their wives near their fixed time. And how much? Ravina said: a season (עונה). And how much is a season? Either a day or a night. And it is explained in tractate Niddah: if she is accustomed to see blood at midday or at the tenth hour or at the eleventh of the day, he is obligated to separate the entire day but not the entire night belonging to it, for she is permitted to engage in relations the entire night. Or if she was accustomed to see at the second hour of the day, that hour is forbidden for relations but the entire night she is permitted; and if she is accustomed to see at night, even at the end of the night, she is forbidden to engage in relations that entire night, but the entire day preceding the night she is permitted; and even if she is accustomed to see at the second hour of the night, she need not separate from her husband except that first hour of the night alone, and the entire day preceding it is permitted. And anyone who does not separate from his wife near her fixed time — even if he has children like the sons of Aaron, they die, as it is said: ״והזרתם את בני ישראל״ — 'and you shall separate the children of Israel' — and it is written: ״והדוה בנדתה״ — 'and in her impurity she is impure' — and immediately after it: ״אחרי מות שני בני אהרן״ — 'after the death of the two sons of Aaron' — that is to say, even if he had beforehand children as important as the sons of Aaron, they die for the sin of their father. As it is said: ״והזרתם״ — 'and you shall separate' — that is, you are obligated to warn the children of Israel that they keep apart from their wives near their fixed time, so that they do not come upon a menstruating woman (נדה); and if not, their children die, just as the sons of Aaron died during their father's lifetime."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:25:43.411569177Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}